WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.462 --> 00:00:01.394
- Good morning, Believenation!

00:00:01.394 --> 00:00:02.658
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.658 --> 00:00:05.527
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.527 --> 00:00:08.387
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:08.387 --> 00:00:10.469
So, to help you on your
journey today's message

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:13.242
is choose your own path.

00:00:13.242 --> 00:00:15.051
Over to you, Michelle Obama.

00:00:15.051 --> 00:00:16.999
(rooster crowing)

00:00:16.999 --> 00:00:19.666
(hip hop music)

00:00:27.648 --> 00:00:30.778
- I want you all to stay
true to the most real,

00:00:30.778 --> 00:00:35.342
most sincere, most authentic
parts of yourselves.

00:00:35.342 --> 00:00:38.638
I want you to ask those basic questions.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.893
Who do you want to be?

00:00:40.893 --> 00:00:43.034
What inspires you?

00:00:43.034 --> 00:00:45.614
How do you want to give back?

00:00:45.614 --> 00:00:49.669
And then I want you to take a deep breath

00:00:49.669 --> 00:00:53.210
and trust yourselves to
chart your own course

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.509
and make your mark on the world.

00:00:55.509 --> 00:00:58.362
Maybe it feels like you're
supposed to go to law school

00:00:58.362 --> 00:01:02.583
but what you really want
to do is teach little kids.

00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:04.670
Maybe your parents are
expecting you to come back home

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.593
after you graduate but you're feeling

00:01:06.593 --> 00:01:09.449
a pull to travel the world.

00:01:09.449 --> 00:01:13.371
I want you to listen to those thoughts.

00:01:13.371 --> 00:01:18.168
I want you to act with both
your mind but also your heart.

00:01:18.168 --> 00:01:21.095
And no matter what path you choose,

00:01:21.095 --> 00:01:24.512
I want you to make sure
it's you choosing it

00:01:24.512 --> 00:01:26.262
and not someone else.

00:01:28.444 --> 00:01:30.913
- Everyone around you
has a plan for your life.

00:01:30.913 --> 00:01:33.178
Everybody around you; your
parents, your teachers,

00:01:33.178 --> 00:01:36.501
your friends, your
neighbors, your grandparents,

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.407
everybody has an agenda for your time

00:01:38.407 --> 00:01:42.286
and an opinion on what you
should do with your life.

00:01:42.286 --> 00:01:45.528
Where you should go and a lot
of times it's out of love.

00:01:45.528 --> 00:01:46.934
It's out of genuine care

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.408
and wanting to see you be successful.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.895
But success looks different
to different people.

00:01:51.895 --> 00:01:54.100
And so, a lot of people
what ends up happening is

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.656
they live their parent's
version of their lives,

00:01:56.656 --> 00:01:58.531
their grandparent's
version of their lives.

00:01:58.531 --> 00:02:02.649
They keep going down this path
that is not meant for them.

00:02:02.649 --> 00:02:03.511
And what happens?

00:02:03.511 --> 00:02:05.434
You may have some success but ultimately

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:06.544
you're not going to be happy.

00:02:06.544 --> 00:02:08.493
Cause you're not doing the
thing that's inside of you.

00:02:08.493 --> 00:02:10.461
And then what happens is
people start complaining.

00:02:10.461 --> 00:02:13.582
Well, I'm stuck on this path
because my parents made me

00:02:13.582 --> 00:02:16.498
and now I have to go down this job line

00:02:16.498 --> 00:02:18.087
that I don't want to do.

00:02:18.087 --> 00:02:21.236
At some point, you have
to decide when you're

00:02:21.236 --> 00:02:23.561
going to live your version of your life

00:02:23.561 --> 00:02:25.927
instead of your parents
or somebody else's.

00:02:25.927 --> 00:02:26.760
Right?

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.654
When you're growing up, you
have to listen to your parents.

00:02:28.654 --> 00:02:29.487
Right?

00:02:29.487 --> 00:02:31.627
When you're five years old,
you're not going to leave home

00:02:31.627 --> 00:02:34.610
and say I'm going to go
forge my own path, right?

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.642
You're listening to your
parents and you adopt

00:02:36.642 --> 00:02:39.115
some of their beliefs and
some of their mindsets

00:02:39.115 --> 00:02:41.264
and some of those may be limiting.

00:02:41.264 --> 00:02:44.061
But, at some point in time,
whether it's at 12 years old

00:02:44.061 --> 00:02:48.565
or 16 years old or 18
years old or 34 years old,

00:02:48.565 --> 00:02:50.959
at some point you have to start

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:52.704
making decisions for yourself.

00:02:52.704 --> 00:02:55.155
And say, "You know what, this
path that you want for me

00:02:55.155 --> 00:02:57.362
is not the path that I want for myself.

00:02:57.362 --> 00:03:00.100
I want to go and do this
and I get that you want me

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.037
to do something else and
that it's all out of love

00:03:02.037 --> 00:03:03.691
but I need to go down this path.

00:03:03.691 --> 00:03:06.740
And even if I fail, I
at least need to know."

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.955
So, if you're not happy
with where you're at.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.228
You're not happy with the
job path that you're at.

00:03:11.228 --> 00:03:13.367
You're not happy with the
relationship path that you're on.

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:16.829
Don't default to blaming other people.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.183
It's not your parent's fault anymore.

00:03:19.183 --> 00:03:21.494
It's not your community's fault anymore.

00:03:21.494 --> 00:03:22.408
You're an adult.

00:03:22.408 --> 00:03:23.696
Take responsibility.

00:03:23.696 --> 00:03:26.585
If you are unhappy with
where you are at in life,

00:03:26.585 --> 00:03:28.272
it's on you to fix it.

00:03:28.272 --> 00:03:30.599
And that sucks at the start.

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:33.455
It's so easy to complain
and to blame somebody else.

00:03:33.455 --> 00:03:35.434
It would be great to
point the finger and say

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:38.201
it's the president's fault
why you're not successful.

00:03:38.201 --> 00:03:42.049
That's convenient and easy
but it's not the truth.

00:03:42.049 --> 00:03:43.740
And when you accept that it's on you

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.724
and you take accountability
and responsibility

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:48.288
for where you are then
you will also recognize

00:03:48.288 --> 00:03:50.844
that you have the ability
and you have the power

00:03:50.844 --> 00:03:54.447
to change it in a much
more positive direction.

00:03:54.447 --> 00:03:55.737
So, the question of the day is:

00:03:55.737 --> 00:03:58.454
I'm curious, what was
the moment in your life

00:03:58.454 --> 00:04:02.455
that you decided that you would
go and shape your own path?

00:04:02.455 --> 00:04:03.288
When was that?

00:04:03.288 --> 00:04:04.527
Tell me your story.

00:04:04.527 --> 00:04:05.762
Share it down in the comments below.

00:04:05.762 --> 00:04:06.987
Super curious to find out.

00:04:06.987 --> 00:04:09.227
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Jane Cassell.

00:04:09.227 --> 00:04:11.487
Jane, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:11.487 --> 00:04:14.946
Your One Word, and posting
it on Twitter and LinkedIn.

00:04:14.946 --> 00:04:17.398
I really, really appreciate
the support and I'm glad

00:04:17.398 --> 00:04:19.000
that you enjoyed the read.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.548
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:20.548 --> 00:04:21.862
I believe in you.

00:04:21.862 --> 00:04:23.708
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:25.199
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:28.259
Much love and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:31.178
for another shot of enspresso.

00:04:31.178 --> 00:04:33.845
(hip hop music)

00:04:40.827 --> 00:04:41.660
- But, see what is the choice?

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.823
That you walk the path like everyone else

00:04:45.823 --> 00:04:49.321
dressed in suits, go
to work, and come back,

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.058
and never have a legacy.

00:04:51.058 --> 00:04:55.225
Or you swim upstream like
a trout against the norm

00:04:56.243 --> 00:04:59.760
and then whatever little
you achieve is only yours.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.334
It's not like everyone else.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:05.501
And I'd rather have something
that is my path, paved by me.

00:05:06.857 --> 00:05:08.891
Something that is my legacy,

00:05:08.891 --> 00:05:11.119
my own self, my own achievement

00:05:11.119 --> 00:05:14.101
than being one of the many
successful people in the world.

00:05:14.101 --> 00:05:16.516
- Every pursuit, no matter
how glamorous it may seem,

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:19.014
no matter how exciting it feels to you,

00:05:19.014 --> 00:05:20.861
no matter how much you feel
like you were born to do it,

00:05:20.861 --> 00:05:22.965
comes with a shit sandwich.

00:05:22.965 --> 00:05:26.164
And so the question is not what do I love?

00:05:26.164 --> 00:05:28.806
The question is what do I
love so much that I don't mind

00:05:28.806 --> 00:05:31.527
eating the shit sandwich that
comes along with that thing?

00:05:31.527 --> 00:05:34.719
So for me, in my life, writing
is the thing that I love.

00:05:34.719 --> 00:05:36.700
And the shit sandwich was the seven years

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.304
that I was not getting published.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:41.655
And that I was coming home from
my job as a diner waitress,

00:05:41.655 --> 00:05:44.131
as a bartender, as an au pair, as somebody

00:05:44.131 --> 00:05:45.989
who worked for flea markets, as a cook.

00:05:45.989 --> 00:05:47.896
And I was coming home tired and smelling

00:05:47.896 --> 00:05:50.003
like other people's french
fries and sitting down

00:05:50.003 --> 00:05:52.464
and doing my real job which was to write.

00:05:52.464 --> 00:05:54.921
And then to go to the mailbox the next day

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:56.555
and get another rejection letter.

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.942
And then say, "Do I
still want to do this?"

00:05:58.942 --> 00:06:00.908
Cause this sandwich sucks.

00:06:00.908 --> 00:06:02.464
(laughter)

00:06:02.464 --> 00:06:04.145
- Am I ready to take another bite?

00:06:04.145 --> 00:06:05.674
- And I did still want to do it.

00:06:05.674 --> 00:06:08.174
And now even as somebody who
makes their living as a writer,

00:06:08.174 --> 00:06:10.466
there's no end to the shit sandwiches.

00:06:10.466 --> 00:06:14.603
It's like, oh hello horrible
review in prominent newspaper.

00:06:14.603 --> 00:06:16.761
That's your shit sandwich today, Liz.

00:06:16.761 --> 00:06:18.012
You still want to do this work?

00:06:18.012 --> 00:06:18.857
- Yep.

00:06:18.857 --> 00:06:19.838
- Yeah, I still do.

00:06:19.838 --> 00:06:20.671
Still worth it.

00:06:20.671 --> 00:06:23.315
Like, hello awful comment on
social media from somebody

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:26.398
who thinks you're a pile of dog shit.

00:06:28.099 --> 00:06:30.406
And just has like chosen every
possible way that they can

00:06:30.406 --> 00:06:32.968
just cannot get it out of
their system fast enough

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.911
how much disregard they
have for your entire life.

00:06:35.911 --> 00:06:37.186
Still want to do this?

00:06:37.186 --> 00:06:38.830
Yeah, I still want to do it.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.831
You know, so that's the question.

00:06:40.831 --> 00:06:42.624
Because if the first time you
encounter the shit sandwich

00:06:42.624 --> 00:06:45.543
you're like, "Well, this isn't worth it."

00:06:45.543 --> 00:06:47.446
Then that's not the thing
you're supposed to be doing.

00:06:47.446 --> 00:06:48.279
- Yes.

00:06:48.279 --> 00:06:50.628
- And there are plenty of
things in life that I have

00:06:50.628 --> 00:06:52.592
run into the shit sandwich
and I've been like,

00:06:52.592 --> 00:06:53.712
"So not worth it."

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:55.115
(laughter)

00:06:55.115 --> 00:06:55.980
So not worth it.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:56.999
Like this is not--

00:06:56.999 --> 00:06:57.832
I don't want to do this.

00:06:57.832 --> 00:06:59.305
Like, whatever the alleged benefits

00:06:59.305 --> 00:07:01.416
of this thing might be, no.

00:07:01.416 --> 00:07:03.277
Soul cycle, no.

00:07:03.277 --> 00:07:04.444
(laughter)

00:07:04.444 --> 00:07:06.753
You know, like I know it's
probably really good for me

00:07:06.753 --> 00:07:08.309
but I feel like throwing up right now

00:07:08.309 --> 00:07:09.371
cause it's just too hard.

00:07:09.371 --> 00:07:11.341
You'll not be seeing me here again.

00:07:11.341 --> 00:07:14.286
You know like, and I love
my sisters at Soul Cycle,

00:07:14.286 --> 00:07:15.685
I just don't like feeling

00:07:15.685 --> 00:07:17.242
like I'm going to throw
up when I exercise.

00:07:17.242 --> 00:07:18.562
So, it's not for me.

00:07:18.562 --> 00:07:21.282
And so that's the question.

00:07:21.282 --> 00:07:23.189
So, if you go into this thing thinking,

00:07:23.189 --> 00:07:26.138
"If I follow my bliss and I live my dream

00:07:26.138 --> 00:07:29.557
and I stand in my truth, then
everything will be great."

00:07:29.557 --> 00:07:31.855
It doesn't mean everything will be great.

00:07:31.855 --> 00:07:33.213
It just means at the end of the day,

00:07:33.213 --> 00:07:34.987
when you check in with
yourself, and you go

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:37.904
in the end, on the balance, is this

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.882
still better than not doing it?

00:07:40.882 --> 00:07:42.639
And the answer is still yeah,

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:44.153
this thing is still
better than not doing it.

00:07:44.153 --> 00:07:45.036
Then you're on the right path.

00:07:45.036 --> 00:07:47.880
- I got into the air force because I was--

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:52.047
As it turns out, I was
romanticizing that whole idea.

00:07:56.171 --> 00:07:59.650
We were fighting World
War II as I was growing up

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:02.483
so we had all these heroic movies.

00:08:04.164 --> 00:08:07.747
And I fell in love with
the idea of flying.

00:08:09.143 --> 00:08:12.393
And then when I got into the Air Force,

00:08:13.778 --> 00:08:16.957
I had this big eye opener that

00:08:16.957 --> 00:08:19.457
racism was rampant there also.

00:08:21.301 --> 00:08:22.884
And that I didn't--

00:08:23.981 --> 00:08:26.481
I'm not as qualified or suited

00:08:29.573 --> 00:08:33.318
is a better word for military life.

00:08:33.318 --> 00:08:37.068
That kind of unquestioning
obedience to a lot

00:08:40.445 --> 00:08:43.982
of things that I think are stupid.

00:08:43.982 --> 00:08:45.676
Didn't quite go over well.

00:08:45.676 --> 00:08:47.191
(laughter)

00:08:47.191 --> 00:08:50.864
So, when I got out I
was an early discharge.

00:08:50.864 --> 00:08:53.114
It was almost dishonorable.

00:08:54.919 --> 00:08:57.524
Because I just really didn't fit.

00:08:57.524 --> 00:08:59.723
But, the catalyst actually was

00:08:59.723 --> 00:09:02.556
I did get to sit in a jet trainer.

00:09:04.943 --> 00:09:07.293
Because I had a lot of people behind me

00:09:07.293 --> 00:09:10.146
to get me into flight school and stuff.

00:09:10.146 --> 00:09:13.478
But sitting there it
occurred to me that this is

00:09:13.478 --> 00:09:15.728
absolutely not what I want.

00:09:17.028 --> 00:09:19.443
It isn't the movies, it's for real.

00:09:19.443 --> 00:09:23.476
This little red button on the joy stick

00:09:23.476 --> 00:09:26.600
controls guns with real bullets.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:29.639
And I sat there for quite a while

00:09:29.639 --> 00:09:32.889
and knew that if I made a strafing run,

00:09:34.023 --> 00:09:37.078
I needed a camera here
and I needed the people

00:09:37.078 --> 00:09:39.408
to be able to get up and
go back to number one.

00:09:39.408 --> 00:09:42.209
(laughter)

00:09:42.209 --> 00:09:45.626
So, I got out of that plane on the runway

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.625
at North Island Air Station,
a naval air station.

00:09:50.625 --> 00:09:54.542
And I walked away from
that and towards acting.

00:09:55.586 --> 00:09:58.745
I knew that it was all about the movies.

00:09:58.745 --> 00:10:00.441
It was all about the movies.

